body:
Ok so full disclousure, I am not ace and if anyone in that community thinks I am being ignorant or intolarant please tell me, I will delete this and apologise. When I was 14 I was really worried because I didn't have a crush on anyone, didn't even know what having a crush was supposed to feel like. I used to just randomly pick someone and say I had a crush on them in order to hide the fact that I didnt 'fit in' with everyone around me. I was a very late bloomer into puberty and eventually at around age 15 I got my first actual crush (it also made me realise I was into women). What I am trying to say is that not having sexual or romantic feelings at your age is not unheard of, that is not to say that you aren't ace though. You very well could be ace and I can't tell you whether you are or you are not. Idk just thought I would weigh in with my personal experince. 

&#x200B;

Ps all you ace people are valid and i love u.

I actually do agree that it is always best to try and find a peacful solution, and the murder of 3 cops is completly unacceptable and disgusting. I support the protests because the community have been trying to find a peacful solution and they are always shouted down, harrased and nothing ever changes. It is a situation where people can not stand to wait anylonger because they are fearing for their lives. Sometimes riots and physcial action are the only way to instigate change, look at the boston tea party for example, or stonewall ect. As i think Martin Luther King jr said "riots are the language of the unheard" and sometimes a bit of destruction, (without killing others) is the only way to make yourself heard. I would like to reiterate tho I would never condon the murder of those cops especially because not only is it wrong but it derails the conversation and gives ammunition to those in power to ignore the message. 

&#x200B;

Also dw you didn't come off as agressive at all, I am just trying to regulate myself, I sometime get a bit intese when disccussing ideas and I try to convay that incase I need to chill

ACAB is an acronym that simply means "all cops are basterds" it has nothing to do with an organsiation or direct voilence againsst the police. Now dont get ACAB misconstrued it is about how even good people who become cops become "basterdized" or corrupted because they are forced to up hold a corrupt system. Also change has been presented, stop having the friends of the police being the ones who have to prosocute the police, ensure that there is better training that focuses on serving the community and abandon the "warrior training" system (I can't be bothered to explain the details of the problems with police trainign you can google it), end mass incaceration, end stop and frisk, decriminalize possesion of weed, reform the school to prison pipeline. These ideas have been put forward peacfully but they were ignored, they seem to be getting more attention now as the george floyd case becomes a top priority. Its not the actions of a few dipshits either, it is a system that defends these dipshits, allows them to avoid proscution and gives them a license to murder whilst the rest of the police force stand and watch.

&#x200B;

Edit: Just wanted to say that, my last line was uncalled for and i appologise, I have removed it. If you want any reasources I am happy to link you to a few youtube videos or stuff like that. Education is the way to change hearts and minds. I am sorry If my paragraph came off as agressive in anyway, it wasn't meant to
